WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.120
Justice League, the latest installment in
the DCEU, is here, and there's plenty to unpack

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.720
once the two hour super-slugfest has ended.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.460
We've got tons of classic characters finally
making their real debuts, we've got teases

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.710
for future movies in the franchise — we've
got the Flash falling down a lot and Batman

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.710
cracking jokes.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.370
"What are your super powers again?"

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.370
"I'm rich."

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.370
What more could you want?

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.400
Well, how about an explanation as to what
that ending was about?

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.340
Without further ado, let's take a dive into
the cinematic waters and explain the ending

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.520
of Justice League.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.940
And just in case you were wondering: spoilers
ahead.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.250
Steppenwolf steps out

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.890
So the Justice League has finally made its
way to the big screen.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:40.600
DC Comics' biggest and best superhero team
has formed, and they've teamed up to fight

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.710
the classic comics villain...Steppenwolf.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.239
Yes, everyone's favorite bad guy, Steppenwolf.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:49.829
Wait, you never heard of Steppenwolf?

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:50.829
Well, don't worry.

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:51.829
Most folks haven't.

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:55.809
To be honest, even most comic book nerds would
be hard pressed to tell you who, exactly,

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:56.809
Steppenwolf is.

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:00.010
All you really need to know is that he's one
of the less exciting henchpeople serving under

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.850
one of DC's biggest bad guys, Darkseid, who
rules over the crappy planet Apokolips.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.890
When Steppenwolf got mobbed by his own Parademon
soldiers at the end of the movie, he boom

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:09.970
tubed his way off of Earth.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:10.970
Where'd he go?

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.000
Well, there's a good bet he went back home
to tell Darkseid that he'd failed to turn

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.640
Earth into a new version of Apokolips with
the three Mother Boxes.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.400
Speaking of which...

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.470
New New Genesis

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:25.660
It's never quite clear what, exactly the three
Mother Boxes are going to do to Earth once

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:29.840
they...well, once they whatever it is they
were doing before Cyborg and Superman split

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.840
them apart.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:33.580
But the comics that inspired elements of the
movie might hold some clues.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.330
While Darkseid and Steppenwolf hang out on
the dank, always-engulfed-in-flames planet

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.049
of Apokolips, they're also at war with their
opposite: New Genesis.

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:45.290
For those who don't know, New Genesis is basically
the jam, and everyone there is super happy

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.340
all the time.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:49.960
In short: New Genesis is good, Apokolips is
bad.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.800
Anyway, it's heavily implied that Steppenwolf's
plan to merge the three Mother Boxes would

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.680
result in Earth becoming a new version of
Apokolips for Darkseid to rule over.

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.370
And when Cyborg and Superman separated the
three Mother Boxes, the area surrounding the

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.490
climactic battle bloomed to life with strange,
alien flowers.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.610
There isn't a whole lot of information to
help us understand what, exactly, happened

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.610
there at the end.

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.519
But could it be that separating the boxes
had the opposite effect?

00:02:12.519 --> 00:02:15.890
Maybe instead of Earth turning into a New
Apokolips, we instead got a glimpse of New

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.879
New Genesis...or maybe the filmmakers just
wanted to make that crummy area around the

00:02:19.879 --> 00:02:23.010
nuclear reactor look nice after the super
people got done punching each other.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.180
Either one.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.829
A league of their own

00:02:25.829 --> 00:02:30.410
The very end of the movie saw the return of
Jesse Eisenberg's Lex Luthor, not to mention

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.059
the first movie appearance of Slade Wilson,
better known as Deathstroke.

00:02:34.059 --> 00:02:37.590
When the two meet up on Luthor's yacht, the
bald nerd says that he'd like to establish

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.739
a league of his own.

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:41.769
And yes, you're not wrong to think he's making
reference to everyone's favorite movie about

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:44.280
ladies playing baseball in the '40s — but
he's not.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.280
Sorry.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.150
In fact, he's referring to a group of supervillains
who, in the comics, would band together to

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.349
try and take over the world from time to time.

00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:54.940
These bad guys have gone through plenty of
different rosters and names over the years:

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:59.870
the Injustice League, the Injustice Gang,
the Legion of Doom, One Direction — we don't

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:03.090
know which name they'll pick when they make
their return in future DCEU films.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.349
But they'll have plenty of heroes to fight.

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:07.719
Room for more?

00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:11.809
Near the very end credits, Bruce, Diana, and
Alfred take a tour of the dilapidated old

00:03:11.809 --> 00:03:16.239
Wayne Manor and start planning their new Justice
League clubhouse — or Hall of Justice, if

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:17.239
you will.

00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:21.139
Bruce mentions a big round table with six
seats, while Diana adds, "with room for more."

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:25.580
Naturally, this implies that more superpowered
folks will be joining the DCEU soon.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.810
It's probably a bit too soon to say who, exactly,
will add their chairs to the table, we do

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.919
have some clues.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:35.209
For instance, Warner Bros. has a Shazam! movie
in the works, not to mention another run at

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:37.689
adapting the Green Lantern characters to the
big screen.

00:03:37.689 --> 00:03:41.609
There are plenty of DC characters who will
supposedly join the members of the Justice

00:03:41.609 --> 00:03:43.919
League at the big table in the not so distant
future.

00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:45.099
Well, probably.

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:48.499
Now, while we're on that subject, let's discuss...

00:03:48.499 --> 00:03:50.919
The future of the DCEU

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:54.170
While Justice League will certainly earn a
whole lot of money for Warner Bros., there

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:58.150
are larger questions at work regarding the
future of the DC Extended Universe.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.999
For instance, out of the five movies that
comprise the cinematic universe, only one

00:04:01.999 --> 00:04:06.419
— Wonder Woman — managed to earn a certified
fresh rating from review aggregator Rotten

00:04:06.419 --> 00:04:07.419
Tomatoes.

00:04:07.419 --> 00:04:11.510
Like Man of Steel, Batman v Superman, and
Suicide Squad before it, Justice League's

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:15.849
score on the site points to an overall consensus
that critics just don't really like the movie

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:16.849
overall.

00:04:16.849 --> 00:04:20.620
While fans of the DCEU might not put much
stock in what the critics have to say, general

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:25.020
audiences might start staying away from DC-based
movies in the future, and that will hurt Warner

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.860
Bros.' ability to continue expanding its cinematic
universe.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.360
In fact, news hit shortly before Justice League
premiered that WB's execs have put production

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:36.300
of the Flash's long-delayed solo movie on
pause while they wait to see what happens

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.639
with its team-up film.

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:40.919
And there's a Joker-focused movie in the works
that will apparently be separate from the

00:04:40.919 --> 00:04:43.050
current slate of interconnected movies.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:46.800
The implications are clear: Warner Bros. is
hedging its bets, and might not be all that

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.259
committed to delivering on the teases that
show up in Justice League at all.

00:04:50.259 --> 00:04:53.680
After all, the end of Dark Knight Rises sure
seemed to indicate that there was plenty of

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.650
room for another batch of movies starring
a new guy as Batman.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:00.800
And DC even tried once before Man of Steel
to kickstart its cinematic universe with Green

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.569
Lantern — and we all remember how that turned
out.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.340
"I know, right?"

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.070
Just because we're five movies deep doesn't
mean that Warner Bros. will keep the DCEU

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:11.389
alive — at least not in its current form.

00:05:11.389 --> 00:05:15.949
It's already got several different interconnected
superhero universes going on network TV, all

00:05:15.949 --> 00:05:19.639
while these movies with the same characters
played by different actors are competing for

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:20.729
fans' affection.

00:05:20.729 --> 00:05:24.819
In the end, Warner Bros. doesn't need to keep
this universe alive, and if the bad reviews

00:05:24.819 --> 00:05:27.710
start to actually affect ticket sales, it
probably won't.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:31.790
Then again, we're still getting Fast and the
Furious movies despite half of them being

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.150
certified rotten...so you never know.

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:35.199
Thanks for watching!

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:37.389
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:39.669
Plus, check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too.

